    "value": "This page documents the step-by-step testing approach for validating Zimmermann's Avalara AvaTax integration on SFCC. It covers credential verification, connection testing, company code validation, address validation, live checkout tax calculation, and Avalara portal verification.\n\nRelated: [SFCC-875](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-875) | Parent TSD: [TSD: Tax — SFCC & Avalara AvaTax](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/355729410) | Gap Analysis: [SFCC-131 — Global-e & AvaTax Gap Analysis](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/362610693)\n\nScope — Which Sites Use Avalara\n-------------------------------\n\nAvalara is used on the 4 domestic sites only. Global-e sites handle tax through Global-e.\n\n| **Site** | **Taxation** | **Avalara Required** | **ATSettings Configured** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ZimmermannAU | Gross | ✅ Yes | ✅ `data/vendor/avalara-site-import/sites/ZimmermannAU/preferences.xml` |\n| ZimmermannUS | Net | ✅ Yes | ❌ Missing — falls back to `companyCode=\"default\"`, empty ship-from (Gap C-2) |\n| ZimmermannEU | Gross | ✅ Yes | ❌ Missing — falls back to `companyCode=\"default\"`, empty ship-from (Gap C-2) |\n| ZimmermannUK | Gross | ✅ Yes | ❌ Missing — falls back to `companyCode=\"default\"`, empty ship-from (Gap C-2) |\n| ZimmermannUSIntl | Global-e | ❌ No | — |\n| ZimmermannEUIntl | Global-e | ❌ No | — |\n| ZimmermannHK | Global-e | ❌ No | — |\n| ZimmermannME | Global-e | ❌ No | — |\n\nPrerequisites — Must Be Done Before Testing\n-------------------------------------------\n\n| **#** | **Prerequisite** | **Status** | **Owner** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Avalara sandbox account number and license key obtained from Avalara POC | ❌ Blocked — awaiting Avalara contact via Tim | Tim / Rebecca Jourdan |\n| 2 | Credentials entered in BM: **Administration > Operations > Services > credentials.avatax.rest** | ❌ Blank — confirmed 04 Sep 2026 | Platform Engineer (once creds obtained) |\n| 3 | Avalara sandbox endpoint confirmed: `https://sandbox-rest.avatax.com/` | ✅ Already set in `data/vendor/avalara-site-import/services.xml` | — |\n| 4 | SCAPI hook execution enabled in BM: **Administration > Global Preferences > Feature Switches** → \"Enable the execution of hooks in Salesforce Commerce API requests\" | ⚠️ Unconfirmed per environment (noted in Gap Analysis H-5) | Platform Engineer |\n| 5 | `ATSettings` preferences configured for ZimmermannUS, ZimmermannEU, ZimmermannUK with correct company codes and ship-from addresses | ❌ Missing (Gap C-2) — blocked on Avalara POC for company codes (OQ-2, OQ-3) | Zimmermann Finance + Accenture |\n\n![avatax-feature-switches.png](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/rest/api/content/475332621/child/attachment/att475758602/download)\n\n*Feature Switches in Business Manager — ensure \"Enable the execution of hooks in Salesforce Commerce API requests\" is checked (highlighted in blue).*\n\nStep 1 — Verify Service Credentials in Business Manager\n-------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe Avalara service credentials (account number and license key) must be entered in Business Manager before any testing can proceed.\n\n1. Log in to Business Manager on `bkzk-004.dx.commercecloud.salesforce.com`\n2. Navigate to **Administration > Operations > Services**\n3. Click the **Credentials** tab\n4. Find and open `credentials.avatax.rest`\n5. Verify the following fields are populated:\n   * **URL:** `https://sandbox-rest.avatax.com/`\n   * **User:** Avalara account number (9-digit number)\n   * **Password:** Avalara license key\n6. Click **Apply** to save\n\n![avatax-credentials.png](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/rest/api/content/475332621/child/attachment/att474906630/download)\n\n*Expected credentials form — URL must point to the sandbox endpoint. User = account number, Password = license key.*\n\n![avatax-service-profile.png](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/rest/api/content/475332621/child/attachment/att473694253/download)\n\n*Expected service configuration — `avatax.rest.all` must be enabled with Communication Log Enabled checked for debugging.*\n\nStep 2 — Test Connection via AvaTax Settings in Business Manager\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe AvaTax BM module has a built-in **Test Connection** button that calls the Avalara API to verify the account number and license key are valid.\n\n1. In Business Manager, select the site to test from the site dropdown (start with **ZimmermannAU**)\n2. Navigate to **Merchant Tools > AvaTax > AvaTax Settings**\n3. Scroll to the **Services** section\n4. Click **Test Connection**\n5. Expected result: A dialog shows *\"Authentication successful — Subscribed AvaTax services: AvaTaxPro, AvaTaxGlobal, AutoAddress, AutoReturns…\"*\n6. If the dialog shows an authentication error, the account number or license key is incorrect — re-check Step 1\n\n![avatax-test-connection.png](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/rest/api/content/475332621/child/attachment/att476053509/download)\n\n*Successful Test Connection dialog — shows active subscriptions associated with the Zimmermann Avalara account.*\n\nStep 3 — Verify Company Code and ATSettings\n-------------------------------------------\n\nEach site must have the correct `ATSettings` custom preference configured, including the `companyCode` that matches what is registered in the Avalara account.\n\n1. In Business Manager, select the site (e.g. **ZimmermannAU**)\n2. Navigate to **Merchant Tools > AvaTax > AvaTax Settings**\n3. Verify the following fields match the expected values:\n\n   | **Field** | **ZimmermannAU (configured)** | **ZimmermannUS (TBC)** | **ZimmermannEU (TBC)** | **ZimmermannUK (TBC)** |\n   | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n   | Company Code | `ZIMMERMANNWEARPTYLIMITED` | ❓ OQ-2 | ❓ OQ-2 | ❓ OQ-2 |\n   | Tax Calculation | Enabled | Enabled | Enabled | Enabled |\n   | Taxation Policy | Gross | Net | Gross | Gross |\n   | Commit Transactions | false (testing only) | false (testing only) | false (testing only) | false (testing only) |\n   | Shipping Tax Code | FR | FR | FR | FR |\n4. In AvaTax Settings, click **Get Companies** — this should return the list of companies registered in the Avalara account. Confirm that the company code set in the preference exists in the list.\n\n![avatax-bm-menu.png](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/rest/api/content/475332621/child/attachment/att476086274/download)\n\n*AvaTax menu in Business Manager under Merchant Tools — includes AvaTax Settings, Reconcile Orders, and AvaTax Help.*\n\nStep 4 — Validate Ship-from Address\n-----------------------------------\n\nThe ship-from address configured in `ATSettings` must be valid — Avalara uses it to determine the tax nexus and calculate the origin side of tax transactions.\n\n1. In BM, navigate to **Merchant Tools > AvaTax > AvaTax Settings** for each domestic site\n2. In the **Address Details** section, verify the ship-from fields:\n   * **ZimmermannAU:** 115-151 Dunning Avenue, Sydney NSW 2018, AU ✅ (already configured)\n   * **ZimmermannUS:** TBC — awaiting Zimmermann Ops (OQ-3)\n   * **ZimmermannEU:** TBC — awaiting Zimmermann Ops (OQ-3)\n   * **ZimmermannUK:** TBC — awaiting Zimmermann Ops (OQ-3)\n3. Click **Validate Ship-from Address** — a successful response confirms the address is recognised by Avalara\n4. If address validation fails, correct the address fields and retry before proceeding to checkout testing\n\n**Note:** Avalara address validation is only available for US and Canadian addresses. For AU, EU, and UK addresses the validate button may not return a validated response — this is expected behaviour. What matters for non-US/CA addresses is that the ship-from fields are correctly populated, not that they pass Avalara's validation endpoint.\n\nStep 5 — Live Tax Calculation via Checkout Flow\n-----------------------------------------------\n\nThis is the end-to-end test that confirms Avalara is calculating tax correctly during an SFCC checkout.\n\n**Start with ZimmermannUS** — it uses *net* taxation, meaning Avalara calculates and displays tax as a separate line item at checkout. AU, EU, and UK use *gross* taxation (tax is included in the product price), making it harder to visually confirm Avalara is firing vs. a fallback value.\n\n1. Open the Zimmermann dev storefront for the site under test (e.g. `https://zimmermann-dev.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com/us/` for ZimmermannUS)\n2. Add any in-stock product to the cart\n3. Proceed to checkout\n4. Enter a shipping address in a US state with known sales tax, e.g.:\n   * 2000 Main Street, Los Angeles, CA 90001 (California ~9.5% combined rate)\n   * 100 Broadway, New York, NY 10005 (New York ~8.875% combined rate)\n5. Proceed to the order summary / payment step\n6. Observe the tax line item in the order summary\n\n### Expected Results\n\n| **Outcome** | **What It Means** | **Action** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Tax line shows a non-zero amount (e.g. $28.50 for a $300 item in CA) | ✅ Avalara is calculating correctly | Proceed to Step 6 |\n| Tax line shows $0.00 when it should not be zero | ⚠️ Likely a company code mismatch, ATSettings not imported, or missing tax codes on products | Check ATSettings in BM; verify product TaxCode attribute is populated |\n| No tax line appears at all | ❌ Hook is not firing — Avalara cartridge may not be in the cartridge path or SCAPI hooks are disabled | Check cartridge path in BM; verify Feature Switch (Step 0 prerequisite 4) |\n| Checkout fails or throws an error at the tax step | ❌ Service call to Avalara is failing — likely wrong credentials or network issue | Check BM > Administration > Operations > Services > Log for `avatax.rest.all` |\n\nStep 6 — Verify Transaction in Avalara Sandbox Portal\n-----------------------------------------------------\n\nAfter a successful checkout tax calculation, verify the transaction was recorded in Avalara's sandbox portal.\n\n1. Log in to the Avalara sandbox portal at <https://sandbox.admin.avalara.com>\n2. Navigate to **Transactions** and search for the transaction by date or order number\n3. Verify the transaction appears under company `ZIMMERMANNWEARPTYLIMITED`\n4. Confirm the transaction is in **Uncommitted** (Saved) state — this is expected because `commitTransactions: false` is set for testing\n5. Verify the tax codes on each line item match what was sent from SFCC (product TaxCode + shipping code `FR`)\n6. Verify the jurisdictions are correct for the shipping address used\n\n**Important:** Do not enable `commitTransactions: true` until end-to-end testing across all 4 domestic sites is complete and the go-live cutover date has been agreed with Zimmermann Finance. Committed transactions appear in Avalara's tax filing reports and cannot be trivially reversed. See Gap C-4 in the Gap Analysis.\n\nStep 7 — Repeat for All Domestic Sites\n--------------------------------------\n\nOnce ZimmermannUS testing is confirmed, repeat Steps 3–6 for each remaining domestic site. US and EU/UK have different taxation models:\n\n| **Site** | **Taxation** | **Test Shipping Address** | **What to Look For** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ZimmermannUS | Net | 2000 Main St, Los Angeles CA 90001 | Separate tax line item at checkout (e.g. CA sales tax) |\n| ZimmermannAU | Gross | 10 Hunter Street, Sydney NSW 2000 | GST included in price; verify Avalara transaction appears in portal |\n| ZimmermannEU | Gross | 5 Rue de Rivoli, Paris, 75001, FR | VAT included in price; per-country VAT rates applied correctly |\n| ZimmermannUK | Gross | 10 Downing Street, London SW1A 2AA, GB | UK VAT included; category-level rules applied (e.g. kids' clothing zero-rated) |\n\nOpen Blockers\n-------------\n\n| **ID** | **Blocker** | **Owner** | **Priority** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| OQ-1 | Avalara sandbox credentials (account number + license key) not yet obtained — `credentials.avatax.rest` in BM is blank | Tim / Rebecca Jourdan | 🔴 CRITICAL — blocks all testing |\n| OQ-2 | Avalara company codes for ZimmermannUS, ZimmermannEU, ZimmermannUK unknown | Zimmermann Finance / Avalara POC | 🔴 CRITICAL |\n| OQ-3 | Ship-from addresses for US, EU, UK warehouses/nexus points unknown | Zimmermann Ops | 🔴 CRITICAL |\n| OQ-4 | Go-live cutover plan for enabling `commitTransactions: true` not agreed | Zimmermann Finance + Accenture | 🟡 HIGH — needed before UAT/production |\n| C-3 | `buildTaxContent()` in `int_avatax_svcclient` hardcodes 2019 test params — must be fixed before testing BevAlc flows | Accenture Dev | 🔴 CRITICAL (if BevAlc in scope) |\n\nReferences\n----------\n\n* [SFCC-875 — Avalara: Determine How to Test Cartridge Tax Configuration](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-875)\n* [TSD: Tax — SFCC & Avalara AvaTax](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/355729410)\n* [SFCC-131 — Global-e & AvaTax Gap Analysis](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/362610693)\n* [24-06-2026 Avalara Meeting Notes](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/275480588)\n* Avalara AvaTax for B2C Commerce Headless User Guide v24.1.0 — `vendor/avatax-v24.1.0/documentation/`\n* Sandbox portal: <https://sandbox.admin.avalara.com>"
  }
}"}

